IMPORT prelude

-- Mediation Act 2017 (Singapore) -- when the Act applies to a private mediation (ss 4, 6, 16), staying a lawsuit brought in breach
-- of a mediation agreement (s 8), confidentiality of what is said in mediation (ss 9, 10, 11), and turning a mediated settlement
-- into a court order (s 12).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/4/2022"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MA2017.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 25 of 2021 with effect from
-- 1 April 2022 (to ss 9(3), 10 and 11); the edition note says it incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone who settles a neighbour, family, consumer or business dispute through
-- a private mediator meets its confidentiality rule and its route to a court-enforceable settlement. SCOPED to those provisions.
-- Not encoded: the definitions beyond what the rules use (ss 2, 3), the meaning of "in writing" for clauses incorporated by
-- reference and bills of lading (s 4(5), (6)), the Minister's orders extending or excluding the Act (s 6(4), (5)), the
-- international settlement agreement carve-back (s 6(3)), designation of providers and schemes (s 7), the arbitrator-as-mediator
-- exception (s 9(2)(f)) beyond listing it, the factors a court weighs when granting permission (s 11(2)), which court records a
-- settlement (s 12(6)), and the rule-making powers (ss 13 to 15).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mediation Act 2017 -- private mediation`

§§ `4, 6 and 16 -- does the Act apply to this mediation`

-- s 4(1): a "mediation agreement" is "an agreement by 2 or more persons to refer the whole or part of a dispute ... for mediation";
-- (3) "A mediation agreement must be in writing"; (4) it is in writing "if its content is recorded in any form, whether or not
-- the mediation agreement has been concluded orally, by conduct or by other means".
-- s 6(1): the Act applies to "any mediation conducted under a mediation agreement where (a) the mediation is wholly or partly
-- conducted in Singapore; or (b) the agreement provides that this Act or the law of Singapore is to apply".
-- (2): it does NOT apply to (a) any mediation "conducted under, or provided by or under, any written law"; (b) unless extended by
-- order, "any mediation conducted by, or under a direction by, a court"; (c) anything excluded by ministerial order (not encoded).
-- s 16(1): the Act does not apply to a mediation which commences before 1 November 2017, except (2) where "(a) that mediation is
-- not completed or terminated, and no mediated settlement agreement is made, as at that date; and (b) all the parties to that
-- mediation agree". (3): a mediation commences "on the day when all the parties agree to refer any part of that dispute for
-- mediation".
--
-- Reading: an agreement whose content is recorded in no form is treated as not a "mediation agreement" at all, so s 6(1) is not
-- met. Dates are numbers of the form YYYYMMDD.
DECLARE Mediation HAS
    `there is an agreement to refer the dispute to mediation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is recorded in some form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conducted wholly or partly in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement applies the Act or Singapore law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conducted under a scheme set up by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conducted by or under a direction of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `commenced on` IS A NUMBER
    `still open with no settlement on 1 November 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all parties agreed the Act should apply` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the mediation` IS A Mediation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a mediation agreement` IF
        `the mediation`'s `there is an agreement to refer the dispute to mediation`
    AND `the mediation`'s `the agreement is recorded in some form`

GIVEN `the mediation` IS A Mediation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commencement rule is met` IF
        `the mediation`'s `commenced on` AT LEAST 20171101
    OR  (    `the mediation`'s `still open with no settlement on 1 November 2017`
         AND `the mediation`'s `all parties agreed the Act should apply`)

GIVEN `the mediation` IS A Mediation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the mediation` IF
        `there is a mediation agreement` `the mediation`
    AND (    `the mediation`'s `conducted wholly or partly in Singapore`
         OR  `the mediation`'s `the agreement applies the Act or Singapore law`)
    AND (NOT `the mediation`'s `conducted under a scheme set up by written law`)
    AND (NOT `the mediation`'s `conducted by or under a direction of a court`)
    AND `the commencement rule is met` `the mediation`

§§ `8 -- stay of court proceedings`

-- s 8(1): "Where any party to a mediation agreement institutes any proceedings before a court against any other party to that
-- agreement in respect of any matter which is the subject of that agreement, any party to that agreement may apply to that court
-- to stay the proceedings"; (2) the court "MAY make an order ... staying the proceedings"; (4) "a reference to a party includes a
-- reference to any person claiming through or under a party".
-- The stay is discretionary: nothing in s 8 obliges the court to grant it.
GIVEN `the suit is between parties to the agreement or those claiming through them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the suit concerns a matter the agreement covers` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the applicant is a party or claims through one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a stay may be applied for` IF
        `the suit is between parties to the agreement or those claiming through them`
    AND `the suit concerns a matter the agreement covers`
    AND `the applicant is a party or claims through one`

§§ `9 -- who may be told what was said in mediation`

-- s 9(1): "a person must not disclose any mediation communication relating to a mediation to any third party to the mediation".
-- s 2(1): a "third party" is a person who is not a party, not a mediator for the mediation, and not a mediation service provider;
-- a "mediation communication" is anything said or done, any document prepared or any information provided for the purposes of or in
-- the course of the mediation, including the mediation agreement and the settlement agreement.
-- s 9(2): disclosure to a third party is allowed if (a) made with the consent of "(i) all the parties to the mediation; and (ii) for a
-- mediation communication that is made by a person other than a party ..., the maker"; (b) the content is already public, "other
-- than information that is only in the public domain due to an unlawful disclosure"; (c) reasonable grounds to believe it necessary
-- to prevent or minimise "the danger of injury to any person" or "the abuse, neglect, abandonment or exploitation of any child or
-- young person"; (d) for research, evaluation or education "without revealing, or being likely to reveal" identities; (e) "for the
-- purpose of seeking legal advice"; (f) an arbitrator acting as mediator under the Arbitration Acts; (g) required by court order or
-- required or authorised by written law; (h) to assist a law enforcement agency investigating an offence; (i) to comply with a
-- regulatory authority's request or requirement; (j) the communication "relates to the commission of any offence ... or was made in
-- furtherance of any illegal purpose".
-- s 9(3): "Despite subsection (2)", a person may, with permission of a court or arbitral tribunal under s 11, disclose for (a)
-- enforcing or disputing a settlement, (b) a misconduct complaint against the mediator or another professional participant, (c)
-- discovery, or (d) "any other purpose that the court or arbitral tribunal ... considers justifiable".
--
-- The Act states no offence or penalty for breaching s 9(1); none is encoded.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `another party to the mediation`
    `the mediator`
    `the mediation service provider`
    `a third party`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `consent of all parties, the maker being a party`
    `consent of all parties and of the non-party maker`
    `consent of all parties but not of the non-party maker`
    `consent of some parties only`
    `the content was already public`
    `the content is public only through an unlawful leak`
    `to prevent danger of injury to someone`
    `to prevent abuse or neglect of a child`
    `anonymised research or teaching`
    `research that identifies the speaker`
    `to seek legal advice`
    `an arbitrator acting as mediator under the Arbitration Acts`
    `required by a court order or by written law`
    `to assist a police investigation`
    `to comply with a regulator's requirement`
    `the communication relates to an offence`
    `to tell a journalist`
    `to embarrass the other side`
    `no particular reason`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground is in section 9(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `consent of all parties but not of the non-party maker` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `consent of some parties only` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the content is public only through an unlawful leak` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `research that identifies the speaker` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to tell a journalist` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to embarrass the other side` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no particular reason` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the ground` IS A Ground, `a court or tribunal granted permission under section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a third party` THEN
            `the ground is in section 9(2)` `the ground`
        OR  `a court or tribunal granted permission under section 11`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `10 and 11 -- mediation communications as evidence`

-- s 10: "A mediation communication is not to be admitted in evidence in any court, arbitral or disciplinary proceedings except with
-- the permission of a court or an arbitral tribunal under section 11."
-- Unlike s 9, s 10 has no consent exception: on its words, agreement of every party does not make a mediation communication
-- admissible without permission.
GIVEN `every party consents to admission` IS A BOOLEAN, `a court or tribunal granted permission under section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the communication may be admitted in evidence` IF
    `a court or tribunal granted permission under section 11`

-- s 11(3): where the communication is sought to be disclosed or admitted in proceedings "(a) before a court -- the application must
-- be made to the court before which the proceedings are heard; (b) before an arbitral tribunal -- ... to the arbitral tribunal ...;
-- and (c) in any other case -- ... to the General Division of the High Court".
DECLARE Setting IS ONE OF
    `in court proceedings`
    `in arbitral proceedings`
    `in no pending proceedings`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the court hearing the proceedings`
    `the arbitral tribunal hearing the proceedings`
    `the General Division of the High Court`

GIVEN `the setting` IS A Setting
GIVETH A Forum
DECIDE `where to apply for permission` IS
    CONSIDER `the setting`
    WHEN `in court proceedings` THEN `the court hearing the proceedings`
    WHEN `in arbitral proceedings` THEN `the arbitral tribunal hearing the proceedings`
    WHEN `in no pending proceedings` THEN `the General Division of the High Court`

§§ `12 -- recording a mediated settlement as an order of court`

-- s 12(1): where a mediated settlement agreement "has been made in a mediation in relation to a dispute for which no proceedings have
-- been commenced in a court, any party to the agreement may, with the consent of all the other parties to that agreement, apply to a
-- court to record the agreement as an order of court". (2): within "(a) 8 weeks after the mediated settlement agreement is made; or
-- (b) such longer period as the court may allow".
-- (3): the court MAY record it if "(a) the mediation is administered by a designated mediation service provider or conducted by a
-- certified mediator; (b) the agreement is in writing and signed by or on behalf of all the parties ...; and (c) the agreement
-- contains such information as may be prescribed".
-- (4): the court MAY REFUSE if (a) the agreement is void or voidable (incapacity, fraud, misrepresentation, duress, coercion,
-- mistake or any other ground); (b) the subject matter is not capable of settlement; (c) any term is not capable of enforcement as an
-- order of court; (d) for a dispute involving the welfare or custody of a child, a term "is not in the best interest of the child";
-- or (e) recording would be contrary to public policy.
-- (5): once recorded it "may be enforced in the same manner as a judgment given or an order made by a court".
--
-- Reading: "within 8 weeks" is taken to include the last day of the eighth week, measured here in whole weeks.
DECLARE Settlement HAS
    `court proceedings were already commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all the other parties consent to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks since the settlement was made` IS A NUMBER
    `the court allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `administered by a designated provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conducted by a certified mediator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing and signed for all parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `void or voidable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the subject matter cannot be settled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a term cannot be enforced as a court order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a child term is not in the best interest of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recording would be contrary to public policy` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application may be made` IF
        (NOT `the settlement`'s `court proceedings were already commenced`)
    AND `the settlement`'s `all the other parties consent to the application`
    AND (    `the settlement`'s `weeks since the settlement was made` AT MOST 8
         OR  `the settlement`'s `the court allowed a longer period`)

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may record it` IF
        `the application may be made` `the settlement`
    AND (    `the settlement`'s `administered by a designated provider`
         OR  `the settlement`'s `conducted by a certified mediator`)
    AND `the settlement`'s `in writing and signed for all parties`
    AND `the settlement`'s `contains the prescribed information`

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may refuse to record it` IF
        `the settlement`'s `void or voidable`
    OR  `the settlement`'s `the subject matter cannot be settled`
    OR  `the settlement`'s `a term cannot be enforced as a court order`
    OR  `the settlement`'s `a child term is not in the best interest of the child`
    OR  `the settlement`'s `recording would be contrary to public policy`
